WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.009
Birds of Prey gives viewers a pretty satisfying
and explosive ending But what we know about

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:10.620
the characters in their previous incarnations,
as well as the iconic Gotham City setting,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.060
raises a ton of questions about what did and
didn' happen in the movie.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.100
"Are we ready?"

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.760
Birds of Prey (And the Fantabulous Emancipation
of One Harley Quinn) begins with Harley breaking

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:26.460
the news that Joker has quite literally kicked
her to the curb, explaining the Clown Prince

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.180
of Crime's absence from the film.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.579
Once word gets out that Harley is no longer
under Joker's protection, it spreads fast.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:38.920
Roman Sionis, the crime boss known as Black
Mask, sends all of his men after her.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.520
Plus, the cops and every thug who ever lived
through Harley's abuses are out to get their

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:44.740
pounds of flesh.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.360
And Harley doesn't exactly go into hiding
she blows up Ace Chemicals in a breakup announcement

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.280
to the whole world.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.680
It takes less than 24 hours for all of Gotham
to know that Harley Quinn just sprouted a

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.020
huge target on her head.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.600
It stands to reason Joker must have heard
about it all, too.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.680
In most likelihood he would know all about
the plant explosion, Sionis capturing Quinn,

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.340
the hunt for the Bertinelli diamond and Quinn's
dust-up with the cops.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.960
Assuming he does know what's happening between
Harley and Black Mask, he probably sees it

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:20.000
as a win-win either Harley kills a potential
rival of Joker's, or Sionis cuts off one of

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.640
Joker's loose threads for him.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:26.420
A reasonable enough explanation is that Joker
would likely be content to sit back and let

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:30.900
the carnage unfold, though it's still a bit
hard to believe he wouldn't get involved somehow.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:32.640
That guy loves attention.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.380
In the real world, with Ben Affleck setting
aside the role of Batman and the shaky status

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:42.920
of DCEU's shared narrative, it isn't a huge
surprise that the Dark Knight doesn't make

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:44.520
an appearance in Birds of Prey.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:49.500
But in-universe, considering most of the film
takes place in Gotham City, you've got to

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.720
wonder exactly why he's absent.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.640
"So let me get this straight.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:55.380
You do it dressed like a bat.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.060
Like, an actual bat."

00:01:57.980 --> 00:01:59.320
"It's worked for 20 years in Gotham."

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.980
After making a huge mess by blowing up Ace
Chemicals, Harley assaults over a dozen cops

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:10.869
in the GCPD, lets a bunch of prisoners loose,
and has a violent tussle with armed bikers

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:14.520
in the evidence room, likely tainting every
piece of evidence in there.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.660
There's a killer on the loose, Huntress, shooting
mobsters in the throat with a crossbow.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:25.080
Eventually, the clash between Harley and Black
Mask erupts into a full-scale war in Amusement

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:25.580
Mile.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:30.160
With all that chaos, Batman should have shown
up at some point during the events of Birds

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.160
of Prey, right?

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:35.980
If we had to whip up an explanation for his
absence, maybe he was working with the Justice

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.440
League outside Gotham, maybe on another planet
or in another dimension.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.740
Otherwise, it seems like there's no way he'd
let all this criminal activity happen on his

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:45.240
watch.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:50.819
By the end of the movie, Renee Montoya, Huntress,
and Black Canary have joined forces to become

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:54.140
a more permanent and comics-accurate version
of the Birds of Prey.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:59.140
We see a quick shot of them fighting together,
and though they have new costumes, Montoya

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.320
isn't doing anything special to hide her identity.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.800
It makes us wonder if she'll ever take on
the role she's assumed in the comics: The

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:06.500
Question.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:12.880
In the DC Comics series 52, Renee Montoya
is recruited by the original Question, Vic

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:17.909
Sage, shortly after she quits the GCPD to
help fight a criminal organization called

00:03:17.909 --> 00:03:18.560
Intergang.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:23.720
Sage eventually succumbs to cancer, and Montoya
succeeds him as the Question.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.360
She continues to use the name as well as the
faceless mask, even though Vic Sage is alive

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.440
and well once more in the comics.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.680
If Montoya plans to keep beating up criminals
with the other Birds of Prey, it probably

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.700
wouldn't be a bad idea to wear some kind of
mask.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.319
Otherwise, it won't be long before every crook
in Gotham knows her address and her old co-workers

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.180
at the GCPD make her life a lot tougher..

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:52.080
The thing everyone is after in Birds of Prey
is the Bertinelli Diamond, a special jewel

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:56.450
encoded with the information needed to access
the offshore accounts containing the fortune

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:58.500
of the slaughtered Bertinelli crime family.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:04.040
As the Birds of Prey celebrate retrieving
it at a Mexican restaurant, Harley and Cassandra

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.480
Cain slip out the back door and abscond with
it.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.510
Harley then explains that she pawned the diamond
and used the money to start a new business

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.560
with Cassandra.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.140
Wait, she pawned it?

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:20.380
Considering what Black Mask is willing to
do to get the gem, you would think accessing

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:24.900
and using the data herself would bring Harley
and Cassandra a lot more money than they could

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.840
get from even the most generous jeweler.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:32.260
Harley isn't exactly the most reliable narrator,
so it's more than possible that she's leaving

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:33.340
out some details here.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:37.780
The account information somehow got back to
Huntress so she could reclaim her family's

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.460
fortune to fund the new team, at the very
least.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:46.720
One of the more compelling characters in Birds
of Prey is Dinah Lance, also known as Black

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.220
Canary.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:53.200
We meet her first as a singer in Sionis' club,
and eventually she's promoted to be his driver.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:58.180
Shortly afterward, Renee Montoya comes calling,
and the detective brings up Lance's mother,

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:00.900
who apparently at one time assisted the Gotham
Police.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:06.400
Montoya urges Lance to be more like her mother,
which prompts Lance to remind Montoya that

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:09.000
her mother was killed without any police there
to help her.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:13.940
Montoya insists whatever happened to Lance's
mother wouldn't have happened on her watch.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:19.400
We're never told exactly how Black Canary
gets her sonic scream powers, but the Montoya/Lance

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.940
exchange implies that perhaps Lance was born
with the abilities and that her mother had

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:24.920
them before her.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:30.380
Perhaps her mother actually used the name
Black Canary before her death, and perhaps

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.520
she was a superhero.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:36.040
The comics version of Black Canary notably
inherited the name from her crime-fighting

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:36.540
mother.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:40.840
The origin of the comic book Black Canary
has been changed several times.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:44.400
In some versions, her sonic powers are magical
in nature.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.380
In others, they're the results of experiments.

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:50.870
Birds of Prey ends without us knowing exactly
where Lance's scream comes from.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.650
During Harley's assault on the GCPD, Harley
notices a Wanted poster with Captain Boomerang's

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:00.300
mugshot and says, "Hey, I know that guy!"

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:05.240
She knows him because they helped save the
world together in 2016's Suicide Squad.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:09.280
Choosing Boomerang as the wanted man is interesting
for a couple of reasons.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:15.160
For one, while Joker springs Harley out of
Belle Reeve at the end of Suicide Squad, Boomerang's

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.080
still a prisoner.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:21.340
So, if four years later he's a wanted man
in Gotham, either he's already been released,

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:22.600
or he escaped.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:27.880
And Captain Boomerang's usual stomping ground
is Central City, which is why it's Ezra Miller's

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:30.320
Flash who nabs him in Suicide Squad.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.520
So why's this poster up in Gotham?

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:37.600
One intriguing possibility is that Boomerang
wasn't released and didn't escape.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:42.900
Perhaps he's still working for Amanda Waller's
Task Force X, his work for "The Wall" recently

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:46.220
brought him to Gotham, and the local authorities
weren't informed.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:49.139
It wouldn't be the first time Waller kept
her team's work a secret.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:54.720
In the mid-credits scene in Suicide Squad,
Amanda Waller tells Bruce Wayne,

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:56.060
"You look tired.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.560
You should stop working nights."

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.440
...implying that she knows he's Batman.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:06.120
If Waller has the kind of resources to unearth
that secret, then how could Harley Quinn's

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:09.040
actions in Birds of Prey possibly stay off
her radar?

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:13.760
Waller is not someone who likes it when her
pawns are taken away without her permission.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:18.419
When Joker breaks Harley Quinn out of Belle
Reeve at the end of Suicide Squad, the breakout

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:22.580
would almost definitely be followed by a massive
attempt to get Quinn back.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:27.420
It's likely she would eventually resort to
unleashing the rest of Task Force X to retrieve

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:27.940
her.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:31.340
And, again, Harley doesn't exactly make herself
tough to find.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:36.360
She walks around in broad daylight in Gotham
City, robbing grocery stores and crying over

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:37.920
lost breakfast sandwiches.

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:43.120
It seems likely if Waller wanted Harley back
in Belle Reeve, she'd be in Belle Reeve.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:48.700
Maybe in the upcoming sequel The Suicide Squad
we'll learn exactly why Waller stays her hand.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:50.200
One possibility?

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:55.020
Waller might naturally assume that with Joker
and Harley's bizarre relationship, having

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:58.920
Harley on Task Force X will always invite
Joker's attention.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:03.800
Maybe between Suicide Squad and Birds of Prey,
she decided the risks weren't worth the rewards.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:08.320
Roman Sionis and Victor Zsasz have a strange
relationship.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:13.080
Zsasz is Roman's right-hand man, utterly loyal
to him in every way.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.980
He also seems to love pushing Roman toward
his darker urges, almost daring him to kill

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:20.240
anyone who gets in his way.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:25.250
While we never see any blatant romance between
the characters, there are a number of scenes

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:26.620
when they get very close.

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:31.920
Zsasz in particular expresses a simmering
passion for Sionis — though it isn't clear

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:36.440
if that passion is romantic or part of Zsasz's
obsession with Sionis' violence.

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:42.120
We never get a clear answer, and both are
dead before the credits roll, so it's likely

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:42.840
we never will.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:49.000
There was a partial answer from the actors
themselves, though, in late January 2020.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:53.790
Speaking with Variety, Ewan McGregor first
said the villains' relationship was "very

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:57.580
complicated" and then eventually it was "more
than likely" that they were lovers.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:02.920
Those answers weren't enough for some fans,
who accused the actors of marketing the characters

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:07.400
as potentially being gay while failing to
solidly represent a romantic relationship

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:08.860
between two men on the screen.

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:14.540
By the end of the movie, Harley has run off
to start her own thing with Cassandra Cain,

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:16.640
leaving the Birds of Prey to fend for themselves.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:21.380
So one has to wonder what the relationship
will be now between Harley and the women with

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:24.480
whom she formed a brief, but successful alliance,
if any.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:29.800
On one hand, Harley more than proves in the
final battle against Sionis and his army of

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:33.020
goons that she can be a team player if she's
invested in the goal.

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:37.900
On the other hand, considering her career
trajectory, it seems pretty likely that if

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:42.200
Harley and the Birds of Prey ever cross paths
again, they won't be on the same side.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:47.440
She may have genuinely enjoyed her time with
her new friends, but her alliance with them

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.160
is still largely one of circumstance and convenience.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:55.320
Add to that her theft of Dinah's car and the
fact that Harley is now unquestionably contributing

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:59.580
to the delinquency of a minor, and it'd be
tough to blame the Birds of Prey if they choose

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:01.960
not to pull their punches next time they see
Harley.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:06.380
Dinah and Helena seem to have put their criminal
pasts behind them by teaming with an ex-cop

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:08.120
with a clear sense of right and wrong.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:13.680
Viewers who stuck around until the end of
the credits know there was no post-credits

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:17.620
scene in Birds of Prey, but there some brief
audio.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:21.940
Harley tells us we deserve something for sticking
around for so long and promises to reveal

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:22.820
a secret.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:28.120
She says, "Did you know Batman f–" and then
the audio cuts out.

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:32.920
We don't know for sure what "secret" Harley
was going to reveal, but it seems the most

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:37.260
likely candidate can be found in DC Universe's
Harley Quinn animated series.

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:42.310
The cartoon includes a lot of violence and
profanity you wouldn't expect in, say, the

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:44.420
'90s Batman: The Animated Series.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:49.000
One recurring joke in the series, starting
as early as the series premiere, is Harley's

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.420
insistence that Batman does very inappropriate
things with bats.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:55.720
"Why are you protecting a psychotic clown
who treats you like garbage?"

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:57.220
"Asks the guy who f---s bats."

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:58.620
"He doesn't do that!"

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:03.000
Considering the very noticeable "F" sound
Harley makes before her post-credits audio

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:07.820
cuts out, we're guessing if we heard the whole
thing it would echo her animated counterpart's

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:08.580
beliefs.

